    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453-a1">

                <pb facs="1248" n="1098" xml:id="pg1098"/>

                <head>[Inclosure.—Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">General Cipriano Castro, restorer of
                        Venezuela, and constitutional President of the Republic, in exercise of the
                        powers with which I am vested:</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">decree.</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. The port of Pampatar is hereby
                        constituted the only open port for the importation and exportation of the
                        Island of Margarita, in accordance with the provisions of article 20, Law
                        XIV of the Hacienda Code.</item>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 2. The ultramarine period given in
                        article 225, Law XVI of the Hacienda Code, and counting from the date
                        herewith, is granted for the purposes of carrying out this decree; and at
                        the end of said period the custom-house at Pampatar shall proceed to collect
                        import duties, the same as the other open ports of the Republic.</item>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 3. The executive decree of April 5,
                        1905, is hereby annulled.</item>
                    <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 4. The minister of hacienda and
                        public credit is charged with the execution of this decree.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Given, signed, sealed, etc., etc., etc.</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cipriano
                    Castro.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
